| Cloud severance phase 2 (sign-in / data plane / relay) | this fork has NO ACCOUNT. Phase 1 cut telemetry, updates and notices while sign-in, the api.superset.sh data plane and the relay stayed live; phase 2 cuts all three, and the app boots straight into a workspace with no login screen, no session to expire and no organization service to ask. **The identity is resolved from THIS DISK, once, and frozen** (`main/lib/local-identity/local-org.ts`): the organization id names the directory holding `host.db`, so it is ADOPTED from the one host database on the machine, recorded in `~/.superset/fork-local-org.json`, and never re-derived — a fresh uuid would not merely empty the sidebar, it would leave the companion's anti-rollback ANCHOR (`~/.superset/companion/state-anchor.json`, NOT org-scoped) ahead of a device index that lives INSIDE the org-scoped host.db, and `assertNoRollback` refuses that permanently, killing the one feature this phase exists to protect. Two host databases with no recorded decision FAIL LOUD rather than guess; `auth-token.enc` is consulted only as a tiebreak and is otherwise read-only, since every procedure that WROTE it is deleted. **The transport is severed at one choke point, not at 133 call sites**: `cloud-severed-link.ts` replaces the HTTP link on both cloud tRPC clients and opens no socket ever — it answers `v2Host.list`, `v2Host.listMembers` and `billing.activePlan` from local values (the host row must carry the same `getHostId()` the coordinator uses, or every host-keyed row belongs to a host nothing can reach; `listMembers` is not optional because the device picker intersects against it; the plan is unlocked because a paywall that never gets an answer locks features the user already owns) and REJECTS everything else with the procedure named — rejects, never throws synchronously, because `void ctx.api.x.mutate(...).catch(...)` sites would otherwise escape their own handler. Deleting the call sites instead would have put this fork in confli