ff is a wait. The retry fires by itself when a local host-service appears or is REPLACED (the key carries its secret, because a restarted host-service reuses its preferred port and a ports-only key would miss the very event most likely to unstick a cleanup) and when an owning host's event-bus socket comes back up - an observed reconnect, not a change in the target list, because a remote host's relay URL is derived from ids and reads the same whether that machine is on or off. One sweep runs at a time and a trigger landing mid-sweep queues exactly one rerun for after it settles, so the reconnect that arrives while the pre-reconnect attempt is still failing is never dropped. The toast is raised, replaced and dismissed from what the ROWS still owe rather than from a sweep's own result set (a Retry re-runs a subset, and rows can be exited or restored mid-sweep), and an empty pending set dismisses it without any sweep having to complete, so a toast cannot outlive its debt. A refused action (a main workspace, an unresolvable type, a row that does not exist) cleans up nothing. While the stamp is set, background-session auto-adoption is blocked for that workspace - the host still lists the sessions it has not killed yet, and adoption is precisely what would rebuild panes for the terminals the user just closed. Snooze is timed and its account release is NOT: a snoozed thread returns on its own, but it returns Following, and re-pinning is a manual choice. That asymmetry is deliberate and signed off - the point of snoozing is to stop the thread consuming an account while it waits, and a pin that came back by itself would quietly resume the spend. Un-exiting (restore/unarchive/unsnooze/uncomplete) CANCELS a still-pending cleanup: the user is back in the thread, so killing its remaining terminals and unpinning its account is no longer what they asked for. Only the unstarted part is cancelled - the panes and renderer runtimes went at exit and do not return, and a teardown already in flight on the host finishes; its late answer is discarded because the stamp it quoted is gone (stamp-identity guard, so a re-exit mid-flight is not falsely cleared either) | `(WORKTREE-EXIT-CLEANUP)` |

