937		// --- Recycle Bin (RECYCLE-BIN) --------------------------------------------
938		// Soft delete: lossless and visual-only, exactly like archive — the worktree,
939		// branch, and any running session are untouched. deletedAt makes the thread
940		// bucket "deleted" (checked first in getWorkspaceSidebarBucket), so it leaves
941		// every other lane and surfaces ONLY in the project's Recycle Bin. The real
942		// git destroy is relocated to "Delete permanently" inside the bin.
943	
944		const deleteWorkspace = useCallback(
945			// (RECYCLE-BIN-SESSIONS) `projectId` is `string | null | undefined`: a
946			// session row passes an EXPLICIT null (it has no project), omitting it
947			// falls back to the host record.
948			//
949			// Returns whether the row was actually soft-deleted. BOTH refusals below
950			// (unresolvable type, main workspace) return false so a bulk caller can
951			// keep a refused row selected instead of reporting it as deleted.
